  "text": "The equation \n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n=\n0\n can be written in the form \n(\n𝑥\n+\n𝑝\n)\n2\n=\n𝑞\n.\n Find \n𝑝\n+\n𝑞\n, and solve the equation.\n𝑝\n+\n𝑞\n=\n \n−168 \n,\n𝑥\n=\n−\n8\n±\ni\n \n4√11\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nWe first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n\t\n\t\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n\t\n=\n0\n\n\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n\t\n=\n−\n240\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n\t\n=\n−\n240\n\n\n𝑥\n2\n+\n2\n⋅\n8\n𝑥\n+\n8\n2\n−\n8\n2\n\t\n=\n−\n240\n\n\n(\n𝑥\n+\n8\n)\n2\n−\n64\n\t\n=\n−\n240\n\n\n(\n𝑥\n+\n8\n)\n2\n\t\n=\n−\n176\n\nTherefore, \n𝑝\n=\n8\n,\n𝑞\n=\n−\n176\n,\n and \n𝑝\n+\n𝑞\n=\n−\n168\n.\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n(\n𝑥\n+\n8\n)\n2\n\t\n=\n−\n176\n\n\n𝑥\n+\n8\n\t\n=\n±\n−\n176\n\n\n𝑥\n+\n8\n\t\n=\n±\n−\n16\n⋅\n11\n\n\n𝑥\n+\n8\n\t\n=\n±\n4\n11\ni\n\n\n𝑥\n\t\n=\n−\n8\n±\ni\n4\n11\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, \n𝑥\n=\n−\n8\n+\n4\n11\ni\n and \n𝑥\n=\n−\n8\n−\n4\n11\ni\n."
